{"step_index":1767,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T00:03:59Z","thinking":"**Investigating GraphCalc radius/eccentricity**\n\n`Metric.lean` includes `edist` and `dist`, suggesting a potential connection. Linking `GraphCalc.radius` to Mathlib's `Metric` is possible, but definition bridging may be necessary. Now examining the `GraphCalc.eccentricity` definition for clues.\n\n\n**Exploring universal ball conditions**\n\nThe aim is to prove `radius G + 1 ≤ romanWeight f` directly, circumventing case splits. The strategy focuses on establishing `ballWithin G (romanWeight f - 1) v = univ` for some vertex $v$. This would imply a connection between the ball centered at $v$ with radius `romanWeight f -1` and the entire graph. Analyzing conditions for a ball to be the universal set, using `ballWithin_eq_univ_of_card_add` as a guide. The analysis involves examining the cardinality of the complement of the ball of radius 1 centered at some vertex. The goal is now to establish that this complement has a cardinality less than or equal to `romanWeight f - 2`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python3 -c \"\nimport networkx as nx\nfrom itertools import product\n\n# For connected graphs where W < n:\n# Is there ALWAYS some vertex v with |V \\ B_1(v)| <= W - 2?\n# Note |V \\ B_1(v)| = n - 1 - deg(v).\n# So n - 1 - deg(v) <= W - 2 <=> deg(v) >= n - W + 1 <=> max_deg(G) >= n - W + 1.\n\nfails = 0\nfor n in range(4, 8):\n    for G in nx.graph_atlas_g():\n        if G.number_of_nodes() == n and nx.is_connected(G):\n            nodes = list(G.nodes())\n            max_d = max(G.degree(v) for v in nodes)\n            for assignment in product([0, 1, 2], repeat=n):\n                f = dict(zip(nodes, assignment))\n                if not all(f[v] != 0 or any(f[u] == 2 for u in G.neighbors(v)) for v in nodes):\n                    continue\n                W = sum(assignment)\n                if W < n:\n                    if max_d < n - W + 1:\n                        fails += 1\n                        if fails == 1:\n                            print(f'First fail: n={n}, W={W}, max_d={max_d}, edges={list(G.edges())}')\n\nprint('Fails for |V \\ B_1(v)| <= W - 2:', fails)\n\"","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9","RunPersistent":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Check if 1-ball is enough","toolSummary":"Test max_d >= n - W + 1"}}]}
